@startuml Adapter_FfmpegAdapter
' If any modifications are done to the classes participating in this pattern,
' this diagram must be updated accordingly.

title Adapter Pattern — FfmpegAdapter

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FEFECE
  BorderColor #A80036
}

note as N1
  <b>ADAPTER (Structural)</b>
  IFfmpegTool is the Target interface our
  application expects. The Linux `ffmpeg` binary
  is the Adaptee — invoked via System.Process.
  FfmpegAdapter (Adapter) bridges the two by
  translating ExtractPcmSamplesAsync() into
  Process.Start("ffmpeg", ...) and reading the
  raw PCM output back as float[].
end note

interface IFfmpegTool << Target >> {
  + ExtractPcmSamplesAsync(filePath, ct) : Task<float[]>
}

class FfmpegAdapter << Adapter >> {
  + ExtractPcmSamplesAsync(filePath, ct) : Task<float[]>
}

note right of FfmpegAdapter
  Translates to:
  ffmpeg -ss 30 -t 30 -i <file>
         -f f32le -ac 1 -ar 44100
         <tempPcm> -y
  then reads bytes → float[]
end note

class "ffmpeg (Linux binary)" as Ffmpeg << Adaptee >> {
  + stdin : pipe
  + stdout : pipe
  + stderr : pipe
}

class BaseSpectralAnalyzer << Client >> {
  # FfmpegTool : IFfmpegTool
}

IFfmpegTool     <|.. FfmpegAdapter
FfmpegAdapter   --> Ffmpeg : Process.Start()
BaseSpectralAnalyzer ..> IFfmpegTool : ExtractPcmSamplesAsync()

@enduml
